 # Captain Notes
 
-## Voyage 1 — TodoMVC vanilla JS
+## Voyage 2 — Browser-identity defects
 
 ### State at opening
-- Greenfield project with test infrastructure (cucumber + happy-dom + world.js) already fitted
-- No production code: `index.html`, `js/app.js`, `css/app.css` all absent
-- Dependencies `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` not installed
-- Working tree clean, `main` branch
+- Voyage 1 complete: TodoMVC vanilla JS app implemented, all 31 scenarios pass via happy-dom
+- Cypress acceptance suite (real browser) reports 5 failures due to DOM node detachment
+- Root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` uses `todoList.innerHTML = ...` which destroys and recreates all `<li>` elements on every state change
+- Additional issue: `.toggle` checkbox not hidden during editing (no CSS rule, no `todomvc-app-css` loaded)
 
-### Decisions
-- **Stack**: Vanilla JS (no preprocessors), happy-dom test tier (per existing world.js)
-- **localStorage key**: `todos-vanillajs` (per spec convention: `todos-[framework]`)
-- **Routing**: Native hashchange, no Director library (spec allows this; happy-dom world.js provides synthetic hashchange dispatch)
-- **Scenarios**: 31 scenarios across 6 watch groups covering all spec sections
+### Acceptance failures (fixed spec, must not change test)
+1. "Mark all as completed" — `cy.eq()` fails: toggle-all re-render destroys all `<li>` references
+2. "Clear complete state of all items" — same: toggle-all re-render
+3. "Mark items as complete" — `cy.find()` fails: single toggle triggers `render()` which rebuilds list
+4. "Un-mark items as complete" — same: single toggle re-render
+5. "Hide other controls when editing" — `.toggle` checkbox is visible during editing, should be hidden
 
-### Open questions
-- Does the user want the `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` packages installed before Shipwright work? The template index.html references them via node_modules paths.
-- The `js/app.js` file does not exist yet — Crew must implement all production code.
-- World.js enforces that `index.html` and `js/app.js` exist before any scenario runs; first Crew implementation will need to create both.
+### Decisions
+- **DOM identity**: The app must mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place (toggle class/checkbox) instead of rebuilding via `innerHTML`. This preserves browser-held references.
+- **Editing controls**: `.toggle` checkbox must be hidden when the parent `<li>` has `.editing` class (CSS: `.todo-list li.editing .toggle { display: none; }`)
+- 4 new scenarios added to `features/todos.feature` pinning this behaviour
+- `watchbill.json` created with 2 watches: `watch-dom-identity` and `watch-editing-controls`
 
 ### Next role
-Shipwright → Crew → QM (per watchbill). Boatswain for custody after QM goes green.
\ No newline at end of file
+QM → implement step definitions for the 4 new scenarios, then execute watchbill.
+Crew → fix `render()` to mutate in-place; add CSS rule to hide toggle during editing.
+Boatswain → custody after QM goes green.
